The Search Better activity taught me that there is more to searching online than just typing a question into Google. I learned about different search features, such as autocomplete, fast facts, and advanced searches, that can make finding information easier. I also learned that being more specific with my search words can help me find better results. This is something I can use in my classes when I am researching topics or trying to find reliable information for an assignment. It could also help me in the future when I need to research businesses, customers, or real estate.
The ChatGPT for Beginners, activity helped me learn more about how AI can be used in everyday life. I learned that ChatGPT can help explain confusing topics, come up with ideas, and organize information. I also learned that asking clear questions can make the answers more useful. One thing I found important is that I should still check the information I receive instead of assuming everything is correct. I can use ChatGPT in my classes when I need help understanding something or want to brainstorm ideas for an assignment. In the future, I could also use it to help with business projects, research, and communication.
The Search Engines activity showed me how search engines actually work. I learned that search engines go through websites, organize the information they find, and then use different factors to determine which websites are most relevant to what someone searches for. I never really thought about what happens in the background when I search for something. I usually just type in what I need and look through the results. Now I have a better understanding of how search engines find and organize information. This will be helpful when I am doing research for school or trying to find information about businesses and services.
The SEO Basics activity demonstrated how businesses can use search engine optimization to help people find their websites. I learned that SEO is not just about using keywords. I learned that having good information on a website can help it rank better in search results. Things like how the website is organized and how quickly it loads can also affect how easily people find it. Links from other reliable websites can help too. I thought this was interesting because a business could have a great product or service, but people might not find it if its website is difficult to discover. I could use this knowledge in my future career in business management or real estate. For example, understanding SEO could help me promote a real estate business or make property listings easier for buyers to find. 
